{number: 108}
{title: The Solid Rock}
{key: G}

{start_of_verse: 1}
My [G] hope is built on nothing less
Than [C] Jesus' blood and [D7] righteous-[G] ness;
I dare not trust the sweetest frame,
But [C] wholly lean on [D7] Jesus' [G] name.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
On [G] Christ, the solid [C] Rock, I stand;
All [G] other ground is [D7] sinking sand,
All [G] other ground is [D7] sinking [G] sand.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
When [G] darkness veils His lovely face,
I [C] rest on His un-[D7] changing [G] grace;
In every high and stormy gale,
My [C] anchor holds with-[D7] in the [G] veil.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
His [G] oath, His covenant, His blood,
Sup-[C] port me in the [D7] whelming [G] flood;
When all around my soul gives way,
He [C] then is all my [D7] hope and [G] stay.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
When [G] He shall come with trumpet sound,
Oh, [C] may I then in [D7] Him be [G] found;
Dressed in His righteousness alone,
Fault-[C] less to stand be-[D7] fore the [G] throne.
{end_of_verse}
